+# Overlap tube state C1 — user-run Wan candidate
+
+This new namespace connects the frozen real-spatial overlap mechanism to Wan. The local candidate is CPU/static validated only: no generation model, VAE weights, real codec, real media, GPU or Colab run has executed. The notebook remains SOURCE_SHA=None until the main session publishes and binds an immutable source commit. Old GROW/bridge/MULTI sources and historical results are unchanged.
+
+The fixed source is the same copper-kettle prompt, seed2026092501, Wan2.1-T2V-1.3B revision0fad780a534b6463e45facd96134c9f345acfa5b,181x320x512 at8fps,50 steps,CFG5. OFF / PAYLOAD_MULTI / OVERLAP_MULTI use cloned initial noise and independently copied complete native scheduler histories. Identity of z, history, conditional and unconditional velocity is checked before step25. Both marked arms update25..49 with fresh conditional-clean derivatives; no denoiser or tail gradient, no history reset. Transformer uses supported BF16 else FP16 on CUDA, FP32 on CPU; state, local gradients, CFG and VAE remain FP32. No hardware or exact-Python gate is introduced.
+
+The old four-channel32-bit OKOK FFT-real mean-MSE payload is retained unchanged, eta5520/N44160. Only OVERLAP_MULTI adds the frozen channel4 spatial pilot:1392 active orthonormal coefficients, alpha1/sqrt1392, target L2=1. Its fresh mean-MSE gradient has eta174, then the actual full tensor update is capped at L2=1, never upscaled. The actual payload and pilot tensors are summed before v_cond -= delta/sigma and CFG. Per step, record both losses, pilot raw norm/cap scale, component norms, cross inner product, combined norm/RMS and norm decomposition residual. Across25 steps report sum, sum of squares and maximum of actual component/merged norms. The CPU target norm and real per-step cap are distinct; arms are not total-budget matched. There are50 combined control operations,50 payload autograd calls and25 pilot autograd calls.
+
+C1 retains three source MP4s and15 second-codec views: each arm FULL_RESAVED181 plus CROP4/5/6/7_129. All use libx264/CRF18/yuv420p/8fps. Every primary receiver takes only a saved file, public keys/protocol and frozen VAE. File names, true start, arm, attack labels and writer statistics are not parsed. Each file is actually read, then for all g0..3 the received RGB interval [g,g+1+4*k_g), k_g=floor((L-g-1)/4), is independently VAE re-encoded with cache clearing, posterior mode and Wan mean/std normalization. Whole frames are encoded before spatial ROI projection. This is not a slice of the original latent or a VAE encode of a small ROI.
+
+The common primary regular support is R=floor((L-4)/4): FULL181 uses44, crop129 uses31. Full g0's45th regular observation and crop g0's32nd are retained in normalized tensors but do not enter primary scoring. The earlier full45 receiver is unchanged. All four phases use the frozen B family tau1=1..45, zero/one repeat-or-skip edge, finite source support. Scores are the same FP64 mean SSE with boundary zeros, exact masked template equivalences and global absolute tie tolerance1e-12. The global phase/path output retains all optimal hypotheses. Any missing phase makes SEARCH_INCOMPLETE. No threshold, edit penalty, payload-based tie break, source-offset constraint or oracle completion is introduced.
+
+Every output remains UNCALIBRATED_DIAGNOSTIC, state_path_accepted=False, accepted_payload=False. A unique finite-model minimum is not confidence or proof of real synchronization. The selected representative phase's repeated-payload bits are explicitly diagnostic; accepted bit errors remain unavailable. Posthoc joins retain registered phase/tau, true-path inclusion, canonical event and diagnostic payload errors, including NOPE and wrong-key controls. Partial phase agreement does not imply source start/path recovery. Repeated payload cannot establish that synchronization is necessary.
+
+Fixed primary bookkeeping:3 generation/source files,15 derived files,60 normalized tensors,120 complete phase/key artifacts and repeated-payload reads,30 global searches and60 posthoc rows. Shared public catalogs provide357480 candidate slots,92016 valid path costs and265464 structural exclusions; each phase file preserves all valid costs, full projection, and exact-class references. Terminal6 path searches/6 payload reads and30 saved-oracle references are separate. Model calls are300 Transformer forwards,150 native steps,3 VAE decodes and60 VAE encodes. Source reads3, primary reads15 and quality reads15 are separately counted. Quality reports15 same-view pairs (payload/OFF,overlap/OFF,overlap/payload), RMSE/PSNR without a pass threshold.
+
+Persistence keeps result.json canonical, then derives blind_readouts.json. Per-phase raw gzip and normalized tensor artifacts are atomic and hashed. Child launch/monitor failures clean up a started child before reopening the latest store; unfinished fixed slots become explicit failures. Posthoc/quality never alter the blind file. Generation and media run in separate fresh processes through current sys.executable; the media process loads only the frozen FP32 VAE.
+
+A reserved explicit C2 wrapper is prepared but excluded from C1 Run all: read actual crop129 MP4 (and actual OFF donor for insertion), delete local RGB[64:68), repeat it after frame68, or insert the donor's corresponding four frames; save through the same codec and invoke the blind reader independently on the output. DELETE gives125 frames/R30, repeat/donor insertion gives133/R32. OFF donor content is not a known zero pilot. These are nominal stride4 operations, not arbitrary single-frame edits or proof that real VAE observations equal the CPU row-edit model. C2 was not executed. Position-dependent payload/CRC remains disabled and unverified.
+
+Nine CPU/static tests passed in18.12s, including complete native scheduler trajectories with a synthetic Transformer, actual FP32 pilot gradient/cap/Flow checks, renamed input identity, partial phase failure, both canonical persistence boundaries, parent spawn failure, reserved RGB/codec API fixtures, and notebook static/build equality. Fixtures do not load models or execute a real VAE/codec. The main session's independent closed-form pilot-gradient receipt is cited separately in the local validation file.
